    {
      "id": 9142,
      "name": "Koga",
      "username": "Koga",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-18T00:41:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>With the reprint of Rook City I've found that the Rook City Environment deck didn't get much errata it seems.&nbsp;Cards still says \"the villain character card\" without specifying which villain character card. Both Tony Taurus and Dr. Tremata still only say they're immune to damage from \"heroes\", not \"hero targets\".</p><p>We've already got rulings that when it doesn't specify which villain character card, it means the villain&nbsp;character card&nbsp;with the highest HP and that both Taurus and Tremata are immune to damage from hero targets, but it would have been nice to have that corrected in this reprint.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:51.511Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 5.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 9141,
      "topic_slug": "new-rook-city-errata",
      "display_username": "Koga",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
