      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>With the reprint of Rook City I&#39;ve found that the Rook City Environment deck didn&#39;t get much errata it seems.&nbsp;Cards still says &quot;the villain character card&quot; without specifying which villain character card. Both Tony Taurus and Dr. Tremata still only say they&#39;re immune to damage from &quot;heroes&quot;, not &quot;hero targets&quot;.</p><p>We&#39;ve already got rulings that when it doesn&#39;t specify which villain character card, it means the villain&nbsp;character card&nbsp;with the highest HP and that both Taurus and Tremata are immune to damage from hero targets, but it would have been nice to have that corrected in this reprint.</p>",
